Subject: [PATCH] BOOTCLEAR9050 fix: the boot question and the Teach-page pitch
 sync are called from MainProc (idle too), not DoAllProcess -- EastSun 1008
 'it still reads the old data but no box asked'.

DoAllProcess runs only while SystemStart (MainProc's if), so the first call came at START and was refused as 'running': the box
never showed (10:27 boot with the 10:25 build; first FLOW line only at the 10:51 START). TRAYZTHICK's pitch sync had the same
placement. Both calls moved to MainProc's DoBoostFunctionStepCooling() line (same line); cinitial.cpp comments corrected in place.
tests: test_mainproc_guard.cpp PART 3 drives the real MainProc with SystemStart==false and counts the box by its text (asked on
  the first pass, once) -- the [BC] checks called the function directly and could not see who calls it. mainproc_guard 9/9,
  Flow9050_Tray 137/137, W6_6_Hub, W6_6_CSystemCycle, FP9050_Pure / Index, HT9050_ProdFlow passed. Debug and release linked.
WORKLOG row 202.

